{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110701","id":2844901957,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6pkcJF","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110701","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110701.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110701.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110701","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110701/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110701/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110701/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a29b998428bcbc84f88d4324bff1369f04750d90","number":110701,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[WIP Draft] The HDR mega-PR","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Update:** There is no longer any need for this PR, as many of the PRs that this one combined have been merged into master. #94496 now has all of these merged in!\r\n\r\nThis is a combination of the following PRs, merged in no particular order, for the purpose of testing how these PRs work together:\r\n\r\n- #94496\r\n- #106940\r\n- ~~#106814~~ (coming soon; I need re-cherrypick this)\r\n- #102987\r\n\r\n# Usage\r\n\r\nDownload the editor build artifact from the [Checks page](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110701/checks) of this PR.\r\n\r\n**Note:** Mac OS builds fine if you build it yourself, but fails on Checks, so no build artifact is made.\r\n\r\nThis PR only supports HDR on Windows, Wayland, and Mac OS for now. SDR testing on other platforms is welcome!\r\n\r\n## Windows\r\n\r\nUsage on Windows is the similar to #94496 (the difference is now AgX tonemapper supports HDR):\r\n\r\n1. Set HDR 2D to enabled to ensure consistent 2D rendering between SDR and HDR modes\r\n2. Change rendering driver to d3d12 to avoid vulkan GPU driver issues on Windows\r\n3. Change tonemapper to Linear, Reinhard, or AgX (Filmic and ACES cannot work in HDR)\r\n4. Set `display/window/request_hdr` to enabled!\r\n\r\n## Mac OS\r\n\r\nUsage on Mac OS has its own quirks as this is a very early rough prototype:\r\n\r\n1. Build Mac OS editor locally\r\n2. Set HDR 2D to enabled to ensure consistent 2D rendering between SDR and HDR modes\r\n3. Disable \"Embed game on next play\" under the Game workspace (Embedded windows are currently not supported!)\r\n4. Change tonemapper to Linear, Reinhard, or AgX (Filmic and ACES cannot work in HDR)\r\n5. Set `display/window/request_hdr` to enabled!\r\n6. Note: Sometimes Godot will think that HDR output is supported when it is not.\r\n\r\n## Linux (Wayland)\r\n\r\n1. Enable the wayland server within Godot\r\n2. Set HDR 2D to enabled to ensure consistent 2D rendering between SDR and HDR modes\r\n3. Change tonemapper to Linear, Reinhard, or AgX (Filmic and ACES cannot work in HDR)\r\n4. Set `display/window/request_hdr` to enabled!\r\n\r\n## Player settings (max luminance and brightness)\r\n\r\nBrightness on Windows is controlled by the OS HDR display settings (“SDR content brightness” or “HDR content brightness”). Brightness on Mac OS is controlled also controlled by the brightness display settings.\r\n\r\nMax luminance, used by tonemapping and glow effects, is read from screen information or can be overridden by the player (on Windows only currently) by using the “player facing HDR settings” found in [this demo project](https://github.com/allenwp/godot-hdr-output-test-project). You can also adjust this using the project settings by disabling the  “auto-adjust luminance” settings.\r\n\r\n# Things to try\r\n\r\nPlease give this \"mega-PR\" a try, especially relating to all combinations the following which have been changed:\r\n- Does HDR mode look the same as SDR mode, but with brighter highlights? (It should!)\r\n- Glow (especially the Screen blend mode, which is now influenced by both tonemapper `white` and HDR output max value)\r\n- AgX tonemapping\r\n- HDR output with the Mobile renderer\r\n- Colour adjustments\r\n\r\n# Performance\r\n\r\nOptimizations have not been included in this PR and there is room for improvement. Testing performance would be better done on #94496.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyN